{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1308327-alternative-contagion-origins-brainstorming","id":1308327,"title":"Alternative Contagion Origins [Brainstorming]","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-04-27T10:45:12-07:00","id":1308327,"title":"Alternative Contagion Origins [Brainstorming]","content":"So one of the things which kinda surprised me about the Contagion Chronicles was how clear and direct it was about the nature of the Contagion and where it comes from. I mean, I'm used that in the CofD the exact of nature of things, be it the origin of vampires or the mission of the God Machine, is usually left as somewhat a mystery. The Contagion, however, was explicitly stated to be the sickness of the God Machine- and while why and how the Machine develops such sickness was left open, it still feels too me like it would have been better to not be spelled out due to it sometimes feels like the Factions automatically revolve around the Machine, making it greater than the private cosmologies of each of the splats in the game, and that now matter which splat I want to develop a Contagion for I need to think about how the God Machine gets involved into it, narrowing some &quot;story potential&quot;. Again, it is only my own view- but it did bothered me, so I thought to myself whether the &quot;Sick Machine&quot; explanation is true or not in my games, what other explanations would other splats think about when first stumbling upon the Contagion, and I've decided to share those ideas in here. If someone else has their own ideas, feel free to share them in the thread.<br /> <br /> As for the ideas themselves-<br /> <br /> - &quot;You heard about the Pain Prophet, right? Of course you heard. Sure, most of what he said were mumbling of a madman, but some parts make sense- even too much sense. Ancient beings from bygone age laying their curses upon the world, bringing death, silence, fear and strife into the world? Yeah, that's no plague. Those are our sins, and the curses we gained as payment for them&quot;<br /> <br /> -&quot;We all know that the Embrace can go wrong. I mean, you can do everything right, spill the blood and invoke the will and all of that, and still sometimes things just mess up. The vitae just turn inert, and instead of another Kindred, you get a revenant. But we are not the only ones to carry vitae- people has it, animals has it, even cities has it. It is the very force of life- and sometimes, as it goes corrupted, the very foundations of the world collapse upon themselves&quot;<br /> <br /> -&quot;Think about magath for a second. What is it? It's a spirit, which by devouring the wrong concepts got its Essence diluted to the point it no longer knows what it is. That's how the Contagion works, only in a small scale. We are used to think about Hisil as a mirror of the Flesh, but we also know that the opposite is true. After all, concepts evolve through time- what used to mean peace now means war, what used to be love becomes hate. The Shadow can't keep up, all the ecology goes to hell, and Hisil itself becomes a magath, and with the spirit getting sick, what chances are there for the Flesh?&quot;<br /> <br /> -&quot;This world is a Lie, one told by the Exarchs to keep it asleep. Sure, nothing new- but think about it. This world is a lie- but it is not a perfect lie. That's the reason we can still Awaken to the truth, after all. In fact, it may not even be a good lie. Just look at all of those monsters and spirits and dead things which lurk in the darkness. A good lie requires a certain amount of consistency, but even the gods can get their tongues tangled when they lie too much. The world gets twisted, the laws of physics get broken- but not because the world is sick. It is because the world is Awakening&quot;<br /> <br /> -&quot;What is the Wyrd? Is it a story, where we take the role of heroes and villains? Is it a dream, driving by love and hate and fear and lust? No, it's physics. You can't get something out of nothing. Payment must be given, and pacts must be sealed. The law of equivalent exchange and all of that shit. However, that is only valid for closed systems. What happens when there is a leak? The Wyrd can no longer bind everything. Things form out of nothing. The Wyrd reach out and twists even further. Fate because ill, and the Contagion falls upon us&quot;<br /> <br /> -&quot;It is always the darkest before the Dawn. That's what we tell ourselves, right? All of our lives are one, long, fucking night, without stars or anything to guide us in the darkness. But things change- the world changes. The world is fucked up right now, but it too wish to change. The Divine Fire starts concentrating, but it's too hot. Wastelands spread, the fabric of the world itself collapses- but it is ok. Soon, the night will end- and a New Dawn will shine upon us&quot;<br /> <br /> -&quot;They say that the Vigil is a virus. One person stumbles upon something in the darkness, they tell their friends, they hunt the thing, someone finds the remains, they tell their friends, etc, etc. But turning slasher is also a virus- the Code gets corrupted, murder because casual and then needed. People become monsters, monsters become people. There is nothing supernatural about the Contagion, nothing strange or mysterious. It is just us, just humans, just people who lose their minds to their own obsession, and corrupt the world around them&quot;.<br /> <br /> -&quot;Everything rots in this world. I mean, just look around you- everything dies, leaving ghosts behind. The ghosts then descends into the Great Bellow, where they slowly lose their identities and minds while rotting away fading into the structure of the Underworld. the Chthonic Gods are just incarnations of that rot, reaching out to the living with tainted hands, sucking everything they can in order to escape their demise, to escape being eaten away. You ask what is the Contagion- what do you think it is? It is our own ghosts, drawing us down to hell&quot;<br /> <br /> -&quot;Sekhem burns in everything. It grows, it evolves, it finds new ways. Tormented by the Law of Suffering and the will of the Judges, it has to change, to adapt, to become pure enough and worthy of Duat's grace. Irem was built to refine our Sekhem, purify enough to reach out to the stars and reach Aaru's eternal light. But you also heard what happens without the Law- creatures which exists outside of Judgement, beings like the Poisoned One which ruin the very civilization we live in. Sekhem without Suffering goes wild, mutated and ruined. Worse- it becomes Contagious. That's why we need to follow the Laws of the Judges in this world. That is why we need to suffer.&quot;<br /> <br /> -&quot;When we Fall, things change. I mean, just think about it- we lose access to our angelic powers, we can no longer feed upon faith and sacrifice. Instead, we turn to channels- we develop our form, unlock our Cipher, learn how to exploit reality for our needs. And we do it? We feed upon aether. And what is aether? The waste heat of the Machine- and what is heat? That's right, entropy. The Machine works non stop in order to maintain the order of the world, and we just fuck with it for our own ends, exploit what we want, ruin lives and steal souls. And all of that when only a small, tiny part of the machinery falls apart. What happens when an all Infrastructure- or worse, a huge chunk of the Machine- Falls? That's right, the Contagion&quot;<br /> <br /> -&quot;Our Mother brought us to the world to teach men fear. They are meant to learn that the world is dangerous, that civilization is weak, that no matter how many candles they light, there will always be the darkness outside. Sometimes, they forget their lessons, and we come to teach them. Sometimes, they twist the lessons, and heroes rise. And sometimes, the learn it too well. They take the lessons and use them for their own benefits, against themselves. against us. The Dark Mother grows angry, as her gifts are being abused. Nightmares go wild, dreams bleed, and the boundary between men and monster is crossed. Fear is an infectious disease- and no one is immune to the Mother's wrath&quot;<br /> <br /> -&quot;You know those conspiracies which make experiments upon us? Yeah, so we are not their only subjects. Sure, doing terrible experiments upon people is all fun and games for them, but that's not enough for those selfish fuckers. No, they want more- they want to reshape the very world in their own image. They make experiments- be them huge ceremonies or new terrforming engineering. And just like those experiments usually get out of control when done upon us, the same happens when they are done upon the world- only much more frequently and in a much more destructive way. That's no Contagion- that's pollution. That's the world protesting against the ruin we brought upon it- and we are all to blame&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-27T11:16:12-07:00","id":1308336,"title":"","content":"-&quot;Anime was a mistake.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-27T13:54:51-07:00","id":1308381,"title":"","content":"thank you for making this Lost Light, I'll admit I was disappointed by the straight up &quot;sick God-Machine&quot; answer. I especially like your answer of contagion as hisil magath","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-27T14:41:55-07:00","id":1308389,"title":"","content":"Okay I know everyone and their great grandmas finds the noose anytime someone even subtly implies the Abyss has anything to do with non-mages, but, even if you cut out the Supernal and Mages entirely from a crossover how can you drop the Abyss?<br /> <br /> Especially with the great answer given by Demon!! I think it was the storytellers guide.<br /> <br /> For me I knew what I wanted to do from the start and the teasers and God-Machine stuff and what the Contagion *does* only has made me resolute.<br /> <br /> Im not right, I don't care to be. Anyone who doesn't like this idea just, you know, ignore it! If you don't like mages or the abyss just ignore me, thats fine!<br /> <br /> But this *screams* Abyssal influence to me start to finish. The Contagion is the result of the God-Machine *mining* the Abyss for raw potentiality, It's obsession with running and quantum-entangling timelines requires the impossible and the discarded of reality, what better oil resovoir of pure possibility than the impossible Abyss?<br /> <br /> And again I find the Abyss so menacing and fascinating that, having a way to include it in other games and make it relevant delights me. They do it for the lower depths so why not the Abyss?<br /> <br /> Id always put a players motivations and cosmogical needs first but... *Its the Abyyysss* cmoooon CMOOOOON! Its practically GIFTWRAPPED for delivering Contagion to the world! I mean consider the *Crossways*, if thats not Contagion what is?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7967-scarlet-witch","name":"Scarlet Witch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"498"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-27T21:44:31-07:00","id":1308421,"title":"","content":"I like the idea that the Contagion is the result of a proliferation of Pyros, just because I like the juxtaposition of the GM's drive for control/stability with the Principle apparently reveling in constant change. Even without involving the GM, there's enough similarity between Contagion and Wasteland/Disquiet/Firestorms to imagine that they're connected.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13641-mad_maudlin","name":"Mad_Maudlin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"229"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-27T23:14:40-07:00","id":1308429,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mad_Maudlin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1308327-alternative-contagion-origins-brainstorming?p=1308421#post1308421\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I like the idea that the Contagion is the result of a proliferation of Pyros, just because I like the juxtaposition of the GM's drive for control/stability with the Principle apparently reveling in constant change. Even without involving the GM, there's enough similarity between Contagion and Wasteland/Disquiet/Firestorms to imagine that they're connected.</div> </div> </div> </div>How does Azoth behave again? It's been awhile since I read Promethean but, isn't fire kind of more of a cleansing force, even if the alchemical change of pyros storms can get kinda... body-horrory? Would Azoth be a better fit, for the theme of sickness I mean. I haven't read it in awhile but I'd have thought pyros would be more symmbolic of cleansing and the breaking down and reconfigurement of parts instead of... the decay of Contagion.<br /> <br /> Now, if the Contagion were to continue to mutate and introduce new changes for the sake of it if an oubreak were to go uncontained and left to its own devices for a while? Then yeah, if we were to use mutation as a stronger theme than sickness or unraveling.<br /> <br /> My questions aside, I was blown aback by this idea and I think I even gasped, cuz its such a good idea!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7967-scarlet-witch","name":"Scarlet Witch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"498"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-28T02:34:37-07:00","id":1308446,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Scarlet Witch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1308327-alternative-contagion-origins-brainstorming?p=1308429#post1308429\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Would Azoth be a better fit, for the theme of sickness I mean. I haven't read it in awhile but I'd have thought pyros would be more symmbolic of cleansing and the breaking down and reconfigurement of parts instead of... the decay of Contagion.</div> </div> </div> </div>It might have been different in 1e, but for 2e Pyros is both, Elpis and Flux are two sides to the same phenomena. Azoth is just a highly concentrated version of Pyros, hence why it allows the New Dam, but also generates Flux.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-28T05:50:23-07:00","id":1308463,"title":"","content":"well, pyros requires creatures such as prometheans to keep it under control and lead to change that actually matters. on it's own its just constant change that's bound to end in flux","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24173,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","user":"Primordial newcomer","date":". 04-28-2019, 11:41 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-28T14:11:25-07:00","id":1308525,"title":"","content":"So I've re-read the concepts I wrote, and it occurred to me that we could map those view into the Factions we are already presented with in the book. I mean, the mortal, Mummy and Beast views all fall under the Jeremiad, the Mage, Promethean and Demon belong to the Ship, Hunter works as part of the Cryptocracy, and the Changeling as the Zero Hour. Not sure about Vampire, Werewolf, Geist and Deviant- I mean, they all revolve around &quot;the Contagion as a plague&quot;, which fits the Crucible, even though it works better for Werewolf and Deviant than the other two. For Geist it is more of something inevitable, which works better for the Army. Vampire's view could be interesting to explore as a new Faction- the Contagion as chaos, perhaps? Sometimes, the world just fail. It is not perfect, it can't be predicted and can't be controlled. The Faction could be developed into a False (that is, embracing the chaos) or into a Sworn (each Contagion is unique, and each should be treated differently, depending on the situation).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-28T20:57:37-07:00","id":1308588,"title":"","content":"I would say Deviants as supporters of the Crypto view, mainly that the Contagion is a result of humanity messing with the world, though less in terms of chaos as is the norm","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#b22222\"><b>.</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3742-iceblade44","name":"Iceblade44","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"707"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-29T06:23:27-07:00","id":1308662,"title":"","content":"Mage<br /> <br /> The Time Before is gone. Changed. Edited. Gone. Reality itself is so radically changed beyond recognition.<br /> What if this Contagion is reality's immune system?<br /> Fragments of Time Before violently attacking the reality, trying to infest reality, trying to be real once again.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1191-rosencroft","name":"Rosencroft","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"88"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-20T08:28:35-07:00","id":1342533,"title":"","content":"Stole idea from <span class=\"b-bbcode-user js-bbcode-user\">Guest</span> - Malkavia virus is Kindred specific Contagion strain! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/eek.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"EEK!\" smilieid=\"9\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> This means that Venture are not 'mad with power' - they are '<i>sick</i> with power'! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/eek.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"EEK!\" smilieid=\"9\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> \u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1305479-contagion-in-wtf?p=1342530#post1342530\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And my friend thinks the Malkavia virus is another strain of the Contagion.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 10-20-2019, 11:30 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-20T08:36:13-07:00","id":1342536,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1308327-alternative-contagion-origins-brainstorming?p=1342533#post1342533\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Stole idea from <span class=\"b-bbcode-user js-bbcode-user\">Guest</span> - Malkavia virus is Kindred specific Contagion strain! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/eek.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"EEK!\" smilieid=\"9\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> This means that Venture are not 'mad with power' - they are '<i>sick</i> with power'! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/eek.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"EEK!\" smilieid=\"9\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> \u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>One of the reasons why I feel that saying &quot;the Contagion is a result of corrupted infrastructures&quot; was a very strange and limiting choice. There are so many example for contagious infections through the CofD, and trying to connect them all to the God Machine kinda ruins some of their flavor. For example, having Malkavia a Contagion Strain would mean that that if we wish to stop the Contagion we need to think how the God Machine interacts with the vampires, which kind of infrastructure was corrupted in order to bring forth that plague and combine all kinds of God Machine related phenomena instead of focusing around vampires and their lore. The same for the Geryo, on that note. Instead of focusing on the horrors of supernatural powers getting out of control and the terrors of the Contagion's corruption directly, I need to shove the God Machine into everything- and while I really like the big screw head in general, it makes me feel kinda &quot;meh&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-20T09:29:22-07:00","id":1342543,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar503_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"503\" data-vbnamecard=\"503\">LostLight</a> my friend said that in his campaign, the Contagion is actually several different strains of the same virus. One strain was artificially developed by the God-Machine (or maybe by demons trying to destroy it), one is the kind transmitted by the Geryo and one is the Malkavia virus. He said if you do it that way, you don\u2019t have to connect all the different strains to the God-Machine.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-20T09:41:50-07:00","id":1342546,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1308327-alternative-contagion-origins-brainstorming?p=1342543#post1342543\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar503_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"503\" data-vbnamecard=\"503\">LostLight</a> my friend said that in his campaign, the Contagion is actually several different strains of the same virus. One strain was artificially developed by the God-Machine (or maybe by demons trying to destroy it), one is the kind transmitted by the Geryo and one is the Malkavia virus. He said if you do it that way, you don\u2019t have to connect all the different strains to the God-Machine.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, I was aware that wyrdhamster wasn't suggesting to tie Malkavia to the God Machine. I said that Malkavia is an example for why I think that the canon of &quot;Contagion= God Machine origin&quot; is lacking, IMO.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-20T09:42:33-07:00","id":1342547,"title":"","content":"Oh ok. Thanks. I agree with you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-20T16:59:22-07:00","id":1342605,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1308327-alternative-contagion-origins-brainstorming?p=1342536#post1342536\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One of the reasons why I feel that saying &quot;the Contagion is a result of corrupted infrastructures&quot; was a very strange and limiting choice. There are so many example for contagious infections through the CofD, and trying to connect them all to the God Machine kinda ruins some of their flavor. For example, having Malkavia a Contagion Strain would mean that that if we wish to stop the Contagion we need to think how the God Machine interacts with the vampires, which kind of infrastructure was corrupted in order to bring forth that plague and combine all kinds of God Machine related phenomena instead of focusing around vampires and their lore. The same for the Geryo, on that note. Instead of focusing on the horrors of supernatural powers getting out of control and the terrors of the Contagion's corruption directly, I need to shove the God Machine into everything- and while I really like the big screw head in general, it makes me feel kinda &quot;meh&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>Gonna point out, albet much-belated, that the book does not imply a causal relation from &quot;God-Machine&quot; to &quot;Contagion&quot; any more strongly than any other theory about where the thing that upsets the apple cart comes from.<br /> <br /> This is the vector for a chronicle with a unified focal element for crossover between games whose otherworldly elements have widely varying degrees of connection to and involvement with the world; Mage's cosmology gives the broadest granular view, but the Exarchs inhabit a part of the setting that can only interact with the Phenomenal World through agents, and Mummy's similar zoomed-out lens on cosmogony doesn't undo the fact that the Judges are beyond approach. Meanwhile, Demon's pretty clear that the God-Machine is physical, fallible, and global; if anything was going to serve as the incubator for a many-faceted disease of reality, it'd be the sum collection of Infrastructure, which takes many forms and accomplishes many things but is always weird and always subject to tampering from outside.<br /> <br /> It's not that the Contagion comes from the God-Machine, it's that the Contagion spreads through everything, and in a crossover game like the Contagion Chronicle is build to be, the God-Machine is a particularly well-distributed host superorganism for the Contagion to grow and fester within. When you have a supernatural sickness that takes many forms and spreads through supernatural means, <i>the big buggy magic engine that makes reality work the way it does</i> doesn't get an exception clause built into it for the same reason that demons interact weirdly with Begotten Kinship.<br /> <br /> The games need to interact with each other in a compatible fashion, and &quot;the God-Machine exists but the Contagion hasn't ever managed to insinuate itself into this notoriously-flawed system and thrive, especially not near all the parts that fuck around with time and space&quot; makes demons occupy a weird position in a setting where they are by-default assumed to exist alongside all the other gamelines' characters.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-21T04:05:05-07:00","id":1342684,"title":"","content":"When every Contagion example is centered around an infect Infrastructure, when the views of the Factions revolves around the God Machine being sick, when the guidelines for designing a Contagion speak around revolving around an infected Infrastructure as the source of the Contagion, when Antarctica, the place of pure Contagion, is all about a corrupted machine from before the God Machine, when the developer of Promethean's Nigh Horrors (or one of the writers) says they don't want to make references to the Contagion in their book to avoid referencing the God Machine, when the developers and writers of the book tell you that the God Machine being sick is how the Contagion spreads and there is literally no counterpoint for that explanation through the whole book and everyone just agree that yes, the God Machine exists and it being sick is how everyone gets infected, then you need to have a very creative explanation to say that the God Machine being sick is <i>not</i> the source of the Contagion. The only thing which somehow stands as a counterpoint is the Geryo strain, and even then the writers said that the intention is that the Geryo are tied to the Contagion, and Shunned by the Moon even says that if the Geryo strain is a part of the Contagion, the God Machine was a part of it.<br /> <br /> So yeah, the God Machine is everywhere and sends its tentacles all around the world. I know it, and I even like it- like I said, I do like the big screw head. And yes, having it as the source of the Contagion could help to tie all the splats together- but with Demon being out, the God Machine became a central piece of a certain gameline. Not that I have complain. However, once you do it, and you make it that the God Machine being sick is the Contagion (in practice, at the very least, as again- all Contagion instances require that you start with a corrupted Infrastructure or some other broken part of the Machine), it becomes way too big then it should be. There is no instance of, for example, a Neithian Architecture structure getting corrupted without the touch of the Machine, or that Hisil gets infected and corrupted without a shining gear out there, or anything like that. Personally, I think that the source of the Contagion should have being a mystery- supernatural powers getting out of control, and people get sick by the strange powers of the Contagion. Instead of saying &quot;the God Machine carries the Contagion and spreads it through the world&quot;, the book should have said - in my opinion- &quot;not even the God Machine can resist the corruption of the plague&quot;. Instead of styling infected Infrastructures as the source, they should have been styled as the victims. IMO, the Contagion should have been its own thing, which can infect any supernatural being, can show up everywhere, and that can also infect the God Machine. It should have been another mystery, another horror, something that stands on its own so that I could use it without needing to even say the word &quot;Infrastructure&quot; in the game unless I want to. But that's not really the case.<br /> <br /> In short, when it was made clear that &quot;the God Machine being sick&quot; was the intention of the writers and developers, it also means that if you want to use the Contagion in your game in the way that the writers have intended, you need to put the God Machine in the center of the problem. I think that the book would have been better if it would have taken a different path, such as stating outright that the Contagion is an independent thing. In that way, for example, Father Wolf wouldn't need to &quot;dabble with the powers of the God Machine&quot; in order for the Geryo to be a Contagion strain, it could just be the effect of Father Wolf himself being infected, perhaps the result of his weakening, or the sickness of the Plague King, or something like that without having to need to say the words &quot;God Machine&quot; in a Werewolf book, just so that you could say &quot;Contagion&quot;.<br /> <br /> Again, all personal opinions and such. Tl, dr- I would have preferred to have a less strong connection between the Machine and the Contagion, and that I could, by canon and supported by canon, to have one without the other.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-21T10:22:09-07:00","id":1342743,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1308327-alternative-contagion-origins-brainstorming?p=1342684#post1342684\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When every Contagion example is centered around an infect Infrastructure, when the views of the Factions revolves around the God Machine being sick, when the guidelines for designing a Contagion speak around revolving around an infected Infrastructure as the source of the Contagion, when Antarctica, the place of pure Contagion, is all about a corrupted machine from before the God Machine, when the developer of Promethean's Nigh Horrors (or one of the writers) says they don't want to make references to the Contagion in their book to avoid referencing the God Machine, when the developers and writers of the book tell you that the God Machine being sick is how the Contagion spreads and there is literally no counterpoint for that explanation through the whole book and everyone just agree that yes, the God Machine exists and it being sick is how everyone gets infected, then you need to have a very creative explanation to say that the God Machine being sick is <i>not</i> the source of the Contagion. The only thing which somehow stands as a counterpoint is the Geryo strain, and even then the writers said that the intention is that the Geryo are tied to the Contagion, and Shunned by the Moon even says that if the Geryo strain is a part of the Contagion, the God Machine was a part of it.</div> </div> </div> </div><div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">&quot;Contagion comes in many forms. In one chronicle, <b>it might be the rotten reflection of the God-Machine</b> [\u2026] In another, <b>it may be an antivirus out of control</b> [\u2026] Some chronicles may have the Contagion as <b>a mundane plague, but one that afflicts supernatural beings as easily as it does frail mortals.</b> Other stories might present the Contagion as <b>a weapon, a concentrated blight on a specific populace, or a mutation in the blood, the soul, or the words one speaks</b><b>.</b>&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;The Contagion may be many things, but it is tearing the world we know apart from underneath us, and <b>it may be the fault of you and yours \u2014 the vampires, the werewolves, the hunters, the changelings, and all their other dark kin. If it isn't stopped, our world may change irrevocably</b>, becoming poisonous to its inhabitants; its elements may be dragged into another plane; or corrupted regions from an interstitial dimension may replace part of our own world.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Not every historical record of a cataclysmic event represents the Contagion <b>breaking through into our world through the vector of the God-Machine's Infrastructure</b>, of course.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Carriers are beings of pure Contagion, <b>brought to our world by </b>the intricate lacerations in time and space that Antarctica's ancient devices create. [\u2026] The Carriers may be the devices' old servants, <b>disfigured by Contagion</b> to the point where their creator can no longer recognize them. Given the nature of their creation, <b>both explanations and more could be true</b>.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;In the Contagion Chronicle, <b>a terrible reality-warping plague spreads from </b>the broken Infrastructure of the God-Machine and throws the world into chaos.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;<b>If the Geryo are linked with this world-shaking epidemic,</b> it may be that Father Wolf dabbled with the power of the God-Machine <b>or some early outbreak of the Contagion </b>when creating the First, a decision the god came to regret. <b>Alternatively, the mutating power of the Geryo may simply be a natural fit to the Contagion's chaos-inducing nature</b>, serving as the trigger for a darkness that's always been seething just below the skin of the People.&quot;<br /> <br /> <b>&quot;Q: Will anything on this book be related to the Contagion Chronicle?</b><br /> A: No, for two reasons. First is that the Contagion Chronicle was but a speck in Matthew Dawkin's eye when we were writing this one. Second is that we deliberately steered away from the God-Machine. You can definitely see traces of it, on account of the God-Machine being so cool that the book's writers couldn't resist, but we didn't want to delve too deeply into the God-Machine chronicles for what is very much a Promethean book.&quot;</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> The Contagion, whatever its actual origins, is a thing that warps reality around it and is capable of infecting pieces of the God-Machine, a massive interconnected and inscrutable entity capable of meddling with the flow of time particularly to ensure its own continued existence.<br /> <br /> The Geryo, whatever the truth of their origin, are ancient primal entities whose power is imprecise or ill-contained enough that the collateral damage they inflicted upon reality led Father Wolf to lock them deep within the Border Marches to sleep for an age.<br /> <br /> The Begotten, whom the Geryo strain can infect as easily as werewolves, draw their powers from a primal source filtered through human mythology, and that source is the same part of the world-soul that werewolves are immune to the deleterious effects of by virtue of their connection to the wider world.<br /> <br /> The God-Machine, inclined to secrecy though it is, taps into volatile powers that can have a massive impact on reality if handled improperly and splinters off bits of itself constantly as it does industrial magic, opens and seals gates to other worlds, and alters the inhabitants of the universe in ways that are typically impossible without the long run-up of preparation that cheats physics just so, and it does this at least in part by prognostication and time travel in a setting where ideas can be literally infectious and the physical world can be affected by the stuff of pure thought.<br /> <br /> If you are playing in a Contagion Chronicle game, you are dealing with a setting where the God-Machine exists and is active at the same time as a thing that can affect it as readily as it can affect anything else; the book is clearly written under the assumption that the timeframe players are engaging with is the modern day rather than a historical period like those found in Dark Eras, and even if this was not the case the nature of both the Contagion and its largest host make it plain that assuming the historical origin of the Contagion is tied to the God-Machine just because the God-Machine is definitely sick with it and its purest manifestation appears to have come into the setting through devices the God-Machine <i>tried to eat</i> is a shaky assumption at best.<br /> <br /> If you are playing in a game where the Geryo and the Contagion as it is presented in its Chronicle book both exist, you are playing in a game where the volatile underpinnings of reality are visibly subject to breakdown in a way that is capable of spreading from host to host and even leaping to completely separate vectors, and also a diverse group of world-shaking primordial entities have been freed from their imprisonment within the foremost wall between worlds in the setting (the one that keeps the world of teeming spiritual power from overtaking the physical world as a replacement for the border zone created by the god of boundaries and destroyed/sealed off by that same being's death).<br /> <br /> The Night Horrors book for Promethean \u2014 a game that has, historically, had a lot of tangling up between its core metaphysical Principle and the God-Machine and which includes in its Second Edition corebook a sidebar positing potential relations between them that nevertheless identifies them as separate entities as surely as the Demon Storyteller's Guide's section on Prometheans does \u2014 not making references to <i>the Contagion Chronicle</i> (which is a book dealing with the Contagion in a global context as a thing that has already spread through the God-Machine) does not have any bearing on where the Contagion comes from just because the developers didn't want to get too deep into <i>this thing that exists as its own thing with a big interconnected crossover context attached to major outbreak events</i> in a book whose contents exist to provide antagonists, story hooks, and ludonarrative expansions to the game Promethean: the Created in particular.<br /> <br /> The Contagion exists in a context where it can break the normal rules of reality, disappear from a region for decades at a time, and be completely unheard of until its purpose-built wardens and stewards reach out to the locals in the midst of an outbreak to share what they know. Most of the gamelines make that difficult to plausibly attach to a unified phenomenon that can wind up halfway across the world instead of a series of isolated incidents across the globe. Demon's primary antagonist does not have this problem, because it is a mysterious interconnected edifice that does weird bullshit all the time but generally has an agenda counter to the destruction of reality itself, and the God-Machine is already correctly assumed to be in a constant state of cold war with its rogue operatives and sometimes itself.<br /> <br /> The examples in the book mention the God-Machine because the book is for use with all the gamelines and Demon is one of the lines where the scope of the bigger picture lends itself to events in Antarctica being related to events in San Francisco, but a Contagion outbreak in a place with no established Sworn or False power bases is going to be largely indistinguishable from any other weird one-off incident until the characters pull the thread or let it fester. If you want to use the Contagion without using the larger context it's assumed to inhabit, that's a problem you've created for yourself, but it's <i>entirely </i>possible for you to bring in an instance of the Contagion through vectors other than its most prominent and most active one if you're just using it as seasoning in a gameline that defaults to local or regional scope.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":111,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","user":"Satchel","date":". 10-21-2019, 01:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-21T11:27:39-07:00","id":1342760,"title":"","content":"I agree with <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar503_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"503\" data-vbnamecard=\"503\">LostLight</a> here - <b>Contagion Chronicles</b>, at least in previews, would be much better book when it would present alternative takes to origins of Strains. No need for other mechanics, no need for other setting info - only two pages like 'If you do not want to connect Contagion with God Machine, here are alternatives'. I know <i><b>a lot</b></i> of <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> fans that have problem with <i>over-presentation</i> of God Machine in 2E settings. And I'm one of them. I can really dive from time to time - 'there is cosmic Machine directing Earth' - but sometimes, it looks like more than 50% of 2E settings are about it.<br /> <br /> For me, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar503_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"503\" data-vbnamecard=\"503\">LostLight</a> just should be hired to put those two pages from his fan notes in official book, to opening it more for other canon interpretation of Contagion, IMO. In the end, <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> settings are based on MYSTERY, not one, simple answer for all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-21T12:47:55-07:00","id":1342779,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1308327-alternative-contagion-origins-brainstorming?p=1342760#post1342760\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I can really dive from time to time - 'there is cosmic Machine directing Earth' - but sometimes, it looks like more than 50% of 2E settings are about it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not counting stuff from Demon or the God-Machine Chronicle specifically I can think of maybe two at a stretch, and one of those is an inference from one of Deviant's sample settings. Everything else is on the level of individual story hooks from sidebars.<br /> <br /> The Contagion Chronicle structures its example settings like a mix of the example settings from the God-Machine Chronicle and the sample settings from Deviant, where there's a bunch of weird occult horror stuff happening in different ways in different places, and some of those things in some of those places link to some of those things in some of those other places.<br /> <br /> Above all, the point I'm trying to make is that there is a difference between <i>origin </i>and <i>vector</i>, and that the bulk of the things being leaned on as &quot;The Contagion comes from the God-Machine, so it has no mystery to its origins&quot; are conflating the disease with its carrier.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-21T15:09:54-07:00","id":1342811,"title":"","content":"Look, I promised myself that I won't get into internet fights- they rarely end with anything positive, no one change their opinion and in the end there is only spite. I personally feel that the Contagion Chronicles had way too much focus on the God Machine, and it would have benefited more if it were to give more focus to other vectors- give us a setting example or two which lacks any connection to the Machine, for example. It is not that I say the the God Machine should have never been part of the game- I'm saying it should have been toned down, and we should have gotten actual examples and the discussion of the Contagion corrupting other elements of the game without mentioning its name. Again- that is my opinion, and my reference. I do not disrespect the work of the writers or developers- which is why I waited for the Kickstarter to be over before even making this thread.<br /> <br /> If you think otherwise, Satchel, it is fine- but I would have made different choices, and I think that the book would have benefited from putting less of a focus on the God Machine. You think otherwise? Great! Feel free to disagree- I am not going to argue with you. I made this thread to brainstorm other ideas for how and what the Contagion corrupts. You feel it is irrelevant? No problem. But I would have liked to see other examples of the Contagion erupting without the God Machine being involved- I would have liked that each of the Contagion strains in the game would have explored each strain strictly from the respective game's point of view- a Contagion based around blood and smoke, the madness of Hisil or the lies of the Exarchs- without trying to tie the God Machine into it. Again- my own personal preference and opinion, and as I spent quit a fortune on this Kickstarter, I think that I can at least say as much.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-21T15:52:40-07:00","id":1342819,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1308327-alternative-contagion-origins-brainstorming?p=1342811#post1342811\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Look, I promised myself that I won't get into internet fights- they rarely end with anything positive, no one change their opinion and in the end there is only spite. I personally feel that the Contagion Chronicles had way too much focus on the God Machine, and it would have benefited more if it were to give more focus to other vectors- give us a setting example or two which lacks any connection to the Machine, for example. It is not that I say the the God Machine should have never been part of the game- I'm saying it should have been toned down, and we should have gotten actual examples and the discussion of the Contagion corrupting other elements of the game without mentioning its name. Again- that is my opinion, and my reference. I do not disrespect the work of the writers or developers- which is why I waited for the Kickstarter to be over before even making this thread.<br /> <br /> If you think otherwise, Satchel, it is fine- but I would have made different choices, and I think that the book would have benefited from putting less of a focus on the God Machine. You think otherwise? Great! Feel free to disagree- I am not going to argue with you. I made this thread to brainstorm other ideas for how and what the Contagion corrupts. You feel it is irrelevant? No problem. But I would have liked to see other examples of the Contagion erupting without the God Machine being involved- I would have liked that each of the Contagion strains in the game would have explored each strain strictly from the respective game's point of view- a Contagion based around blood and smoke, the madness of Hisil or the lies of the Exarchs- without trying to tie the God Machine into it. Again- my own personal preference and opinion, and as I spent quit a fortune on this Kickstarter, I think that I can at least say as much.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have no issue with proposing sources for Contagion that aren't tied to Infrastructure \u2014 it's a perfectly valid and admirable pursuit that helps substantially with framing smaller-scale outbreaks for less crossover-intensive games.<br /> <br /> My issue is with spreading misinformation of the sort I was already sick of seeing before the Revised Storytelling System was a thing, which you do when you insist that the reading your work is premised on is correct because the God-Machine is touching much of the sample settings through its opposition to and subversion by the Contagion.<br /> <br /> Can you acknowledge that the book does not posit the God-Machine as the actual origin of the Contagion any more than it posits a concrete origin point for the God-Machine itself? Because I'm content to sit back and let the thread get back to its nominal purpose and we have no problem if so, but I draw the line at complaints founded in the same &quot;2e says God-Machine did it&quot; misreadings that were endemic to these forums circa 2014 when the Contagion Chronicle's predecessor bluebook came out.<br /> <br /> Nothing about making Contagion outbreaks particular to individual gamelines' perspectives requires people to think that the Contagion is <i>just</i> an infection of the God-Machine, much less that it <i>is</i> the God-Machine going haywire and nothing more. You're welcome to make Contagions derived from mutant Strix or Sybaris or Flux or the Year of Plague or any other occult hotbed of mutation you care to name, and I wholeheartedly support your endeavor to do so, but you're not &quot;breaking from canon&quot; when you do so.<br /> <br /> That is all.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-21T16:03:06-07:00","id":1342821,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1308327-alternative-contagion-origins-brainstorming?p=1342779#post1342779\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not counting stuff from Demon or the God-Machine Chronicle specifically I can think of maybe two at a stretch, and one of those is an inference from one of Deviant's sample settings. Everything else is on the level of individual story hooks from sidebars.<br /> <br /> The Contagion Chronicle structures its example settings like a mix of the example settings from the God-Machine Chronicle and the sample settings from Deviant, where there's a bunch of weird occult horror stuff happening in different ways in different places, and some of those things in some of those places link to some of those things in some of those other places.<br /> <br /> Above all, the point I'm trying to make is that there is a difference between <i>origin </i>and <i>vector</i>, and that the bulk of the things being leaned on as &quot;The Contagion comes from the God-Machine, so it has no mystery to its origins&quot; are conflating the disease with its carrier.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;I may have the plague and may thus give the plague, but I'm definitely not the origin of the plague,&quot; in short?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 10-21-2019, 07:05 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-21T16:27:31-07:00","id":1342829,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar111_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"111\" data-vbnamecard=\"111\">Satchel</a> <br /> Very well- the exact words of &quot;the God Machine is the source of the Contagion&quot; are not explicitly stated in the book. The theme of the &quot;God Machine is sick and infects everything and everyone around it&quot;, however, is repeated throw the book. It is not the source, it is not the cause, and no, the God Machine &quot;didn't do it&quot;. There is, on the other hand, no support in the book for Contagion strains which do not first come from a corrupted infrastructure or anything like that, and much of the book is based around the notion of the God Machine being sick is how the Contagion spreads. When we have 12 settings and all of them speak about how the Contagion starts from some broken gear of some kind, I can't see how can you say that the canon supports a strain which does not involve the God Machine. The way I see it, it is clearly the intention of the writers that every Contagion outburst should come from the God Machine, be it the cause of it or its patient zero. For me, if the God Machine is always the first thing to get corrupted and that corruption somehow shapes the Contagion's outburst, it is no different from it being the cause IMO. I would have liked the Contagion being its own thing, talking about the God Machine as little as the Principle, the Exarchs or any other Power that's Be in the book. If you call that a misinformation, I can't see it- again, I read the book just as you did, and that's the impression that I got.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-21T17:56:39-07:00","id":1342845,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1308327-alternative-contagion-origins-brainstorming?p=1342829#post1342829\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar111_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"111\" data-vbnamecard=\"111\">Satchel</a><br /> Very well- the exact words of &quot;the God Machine is the source of the Contagion&quot; are not explicitly stated in the book. The theme of the &quot;God Machine is sick and infects everything and everyone around it&quot;, however, is repeated throw the book. It is not the source, it is not the cause, and no, the God Machine &quot;didn't do it&quot;. There is, on the other hand, no support in the book for Contagion strains which do not first come from a corrupted infrastructure or anything like that, and much of the book is based around the notion of the God Machine being sick is how the Contagion spreads. When we have 12 settings and all of them speak about how the Contagion starts from some broken gear of some kind, I can't see how can you say that the canon supports a strain which does not involve the God Machine. The way I see it, it is clearly the intention of the writers that every Contagion outburst should come from the God Machine, be it the cause of it or its patient zero. For me, if the God Machine is always the first thing to get corrupted and that corruption somehow shapes the Contagion's outburst, it is no different from it being the cause IMO. I would have liked the Contagion being its own thing, talking about the God Machine as little as the Principle, the Exarchs or any other Power that's Be in the book. If you call that a misinformation, I can't see it- again, I read the book just as you did, and that's the impression that I got.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is the <i>dumbest</i>-<br /> <br /> No, that's not true, I still have that one gay entitlement* in my head-<br /> <br /> But this is <i>dumb</i>.<br /> <br /> Okay, let's...think about this in terms of real world applications.<br /> <br /> Okay, while on the same reach, I want you to, for the moment, imagine how much UPS, DHL, Amazon, and FedEx reach the whole world. Odds are, you've received a package from one of the four in your lifetime.<br /> <br /> Now imagine those three as one conglomerate.<br /> <br /> Now imagine that conglomerate as being solely dedicated to delivery.<br /> <br /> Now imagine that dediation to delivery is dedicated without too much regard for small details in what it delivers. Big ass problems, no, leave the plutonium and several thousands of gas tanks on the floor, please, but small things, sure.<br /> <br /> Now, imagine if you will, someone, or something, delivered trace elements of a bug, a flu, a virus, something. Imagine, if you will, a lot of someones or somethings had this issue.<br /> <br /> At it's core, you wouldn't be too surprised if all the workers in the delivery, who can't spend too much time worrying if they get sick or not cause <s>Jeff Bezos</s> people need things to get where they are going on time and that's kind of your entire life, end up sick with all sorts things. Some are asymptomatic, some are dying in the corridors of stuff. But it is <i>insane</i> to think no one catches nothing in that process.<br /> <br /> Now imagine, with your various 24 hour deliveries and what not, how those various diseases then begin to spread and propogate. Some go global! Congratulations, you have swine flu from California, with love, enjoy your life in Ghana, Congratulations, you have mad cow disease from Ghana, enjoy your life in California. Some are more heavily concentrated due to immunities and localizations and the lifespan of diseases, so maybe it's just everyone in New Zealand that gets gonorrhea-but-by-touch-instead-of-by-sex. But it's the fact that the delivery systems are all over the fucking world, always processing and delivery, that gets things there.<br /> <br /> Now imagine if that delivery system was, shall we say, more involved with your life. Wanted to manipulate your free will to it's ends, take advantage of your subconscious thoughts, desires, and fears to it's own end. Wanted to make something out of it, and wanted to shape your community.<br /> <br /> I'll stop talking about the delivery systems themselves, but by this comparison, it would be <i>fucking weird</i> to not address the God-Machine as a carrier. The G-M is deliberately a system that involves itself in the lives of every fucking thing, <i>whether they notice it or not</i>. It has more reach in the mortal, material world(that thing that every splat participates in) than the Curses in the Blood, Spiritual Resonance, Supernal Resonance, Azothic Connection, <i>the fucking Wyrd</i>, any Compact or Conspiracy system outside of maybe YouFuckingTube, The Twilight Network, Lifeweb, or Primordial OR Bright Dream <i>by themselves</i>. Combinations of these might approximate that reach as well, but limit the degree of influence as well-the G-M is pretty universal in it's own terms of own materials, from the physical to the emotional, psychological, and spiritual, where as everything else finds some kind of barrier.<br /> <br /> You can make an argument that the G-M was relied on a <i>hair</i> too much, but you can't deny the reason why the G-M, as a infiltrator and contaminant-in-it's-own-right, is a hyper-relevant means of contamination in the world. Maybe one out of thirteen could get away with it, but with fucking affecting the commonal base reality more so than anything else so pervasively, the G-M <i>just makes sense</i>.<br /> <br /> And mind you, that's it as a carrier, because at no point does being the carrier <i>make you the god damn origin, please think on this for a second I implore you</i>.<br /> <br /> Because seriously, none of that delivery system analogy pins the blame of origin <i>on </i>the delivery system. The Contagion has the freedom to be from anywhere-but it's unrealistic that it's delivery system doesn't have <i>something to do </i>with the God-Machine <i>unless</i> the Contagion in question is specialized.<br /> <br /> I have <i>five</i> Contagions I have boiling in the background of my two more pertinent projects, and without even glancing at them, I could tell you all of them, each uniquely crafted, could be communicated by the G-M and, likewise, <i>have nothing to do with the G-M asides from the convience of it as a carrier</i>. It would, therefore, be weird <i>not to account for that.</i><br /> <br /> <i>Please think about this.</i><br /> <br /> *Gay elves being gay in a treehouse together, imagine.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 10-21-2019, 11:54 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-22T00:08:31-07:00","id":1342890,"title":"","content":"Aaaaaaaaand I had enough. Let's put it this way- I both agree with you on the conceptual level that yes, it makes sense, and I tell you that on the overall level, I think that it could have been done better. There could have been a different presentation, a different focus, and that I don't like the way it was done. If you call &quot;thinking that they put too much focus on the God Machine for a Crossover Chronicles&quot; dumb, we apparently have nothing to discuss with each other on this subject. We also apparently have different ways to operate the CofD, as in mine the God Machine, while very dominant and spread in the world, is far from without contenders.<br /> <br /> So yeah, no- I don't think it is an irrational thing to ask to actually give an equal place to each splat in a <i>Crossover Chronicles</i>,<br /> <br /> And I'm done replying to this subject. I can see that nothing good is going to come out of it for me, and I'm walking out.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-22T01:32:45-07:00","id":1342904,"title":"","content":"Let's return to topic subject - i.e. <b>talking about alternative origins for Contagion phenomena </b>- that was opening idea of the topic. Those not agreeing with idea of alternative origins, just can easily stay out of this topic. And everyone will be happy then! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-28T04:07:56-07:00","id":1376946,"title":"","content":"Now that the previews from Mummy has expanded upon the pyramid under the Ronne Ice Shelf, has anyone done anything to the Antarctica settings in Contagion Chronicle and Mummy? I'm asking here because it's the only setting (that I know of, haven't read all of them) that doesn't directly involve the God-Machine since it's a different (though similar and likely related) machine that is the cause/patient zero of this outbreak.<br /> <br /> I've been thinking about STing a game in Antarctica sometime in the future when I'm no longer busy GMing another game, and if I do I'd like to focus on the whole alternate timeline/history angle, stuff like Carriers with memories that diverge from RL, the manifestations of jungles implied to be from the continent's past (i.e. Gondwana), artifacts that show up as belonging to different times under Mage Sight, and a pyramid from an empire that was erased from existence (though a lot of artefacts from the Nameless Empire does naturally persist without the Contagion).<br /> I'm leaning towards having the ancient device be part of a plan for the Carriers to escape their doomed timeline by shifting it into our world. Problem is that most individual Carriers doesn't know that much about that plan, nor does it help that they absorb different memories when they go The Thing on humans. The Contagion might be part of the plan, an unintended side effect, or possibly the end result gone wrong and the plan simply does not work (but it will fuck up the world anyway). The pyramid could then be part of the failure of Second Irem, when they accidentally activated the ancient device and displaced the whole thing so that it never disappeared with the rest of the Nameless Empire.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-28T06:03:39-07:00","id":1376952,"title":"","content":"I read A Thousand and One Nightmares in Dark Eras 2 and it made me think that the Contagion must have some connection to the Dark Mother from B:tP. Aren\u2019t the God-Machine and the Dark Mother enemies?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-28T08:22:39-07:00","id":1376964,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1308327-alternative-contagion-origins-brainstorming?p=1376952#post1376952\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Aren\u2019t the God-Machine and the Dark Mother enemies?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes and no. They generally operate on different strata of <b>CoD</b> universe - God-Machine operates in material realm, were he expands. Dark Mother is operating in Astral, where she sends her nightmares on humanity, However, there is pointed in <b>Night Horrors - Conquering Heroes</b> book, in Insatiable chapter, there is <i>Progenitor</i>, male fiugre similar to Dark Mother, but with other agenda. Seeing him as God-Machine is logical connection to see. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-28T09:18:48-07:00","id":1376971,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1437_5.jpg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1437\" data-vbnamecard=\"1437\">wyrdhamster</a> but didn\u2019t the Dark Mother kill the Primogenitor?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]}]}